Confirmed a critical defect: `momentum_signals` (line 911) and `mean_reversion_signals` (line 881) both compute `np.mean(np.log(closes[window]))` — the mean **log price level** — not a return. For any price > 1 this is always positive, so momentum is always +1 (permanently long) and reversal always −1 (permanently short); neither ever flips. This means the "momentum edge" is a static long bias, not a momentum signal. I must substantiate this across the universe before recording it.
